# ===========================================================================
#  What is committed, and why
# ===========================================================================
#  COMMITTED:
#    data/raw/Global Superstore.xls  (17 MB) - the provenance of the entire
#      project. Re-fetching it depends on a third-party repository staying
#      online, and the LFS-pointer problem documented in PROJECT_PROVENANCE.txt
#      makes it non-trivial to find again. Worth the 17 MB.
#    All code, SQL, reports, figures, and the executed notebook with outputs.
#    The small dimension tables - a reviewer can inspect the resolved customers,
#      products and RFM segments without running anything.
#
#  IGNORED: the four large fact tables below (57 MB combined). Every one is
#    regenerated in under a minute by:
#        python src/data_cleaning.py && python src/feature_engineering.py
#    Committing them would add ~57 MB of binary-ish churn on every change to the
#    pipeline while adding nothing a reviewer cannot regenerate.
# ===========================================================================

# Large regenerable fact tables ---------------------------------------------
data/processed/orders_features.csv
data/processed/orders_clean.csv
data/processed/orders_agg.csv
dashboard/data/fact_sales.csv

# Everything else under data/processed and dashboard/data IS tracked:
#   customers.csv, customer_metrics.csv, products.csv, rfm_segments.csv,
#   rfm_segment_summary.csv, cohort_retention.csv, cohort_counts.csv,
#   regional_managers.csv, monthly_kpis.csv
#   dim_date.csv, dim_customer.csv, dim_product.csv, dim_geography.csv,
#   dim_returns_coverage.csv, model_manifest.json
#
# reports/ is tracked in full - the data quality report, the verification
# report and the facts JSONs are the EVIDENCE for the claims in the README.
# Ignoring them would leave the numbers unsupported.

# Power BI ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pbix
*.pbip
.pbi/
**/.pbi/
**/.pbitmp/

# Python --------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Jupyter -------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# NOTE: notebooks/ecommerce_analysis.ipynb is tracked WITH its outputs, on
# purpose. Stripping them would leave a reviewer with 14 empty figure cells
# unless they installed the dependencies and ran the whole pipeline first.

# Editors, tooling, OS ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
